WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.900
The Mississippi state

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:02.268
Senate is considering

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:04.004
a controversial bill

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:06.239
that critics call the 21st century

00:00:06.239 --> 00:00:07.440
Jim Crow.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.074
The area

00:00:08.074 --> 00:00:10.443
near the Capitol government buildings

00:00:10.443 --> 00:00:11.978
right now in Jackson.

00:00:11.978 --> 00:00:13.480
That area has its own district

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:15.315
patrolled by Capitol Police officers.

00:00:15.315 --> 00:00:16.282
Republican lawmakers

00:00:16.282 --> 00:00:17.283
in the state House

00:00:17.283 --> 00:00:18.418
have passed a bill

00:00:18.418 --> 00:00:19.652
that would expand that

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:21.921
specially designated district

00:00:21.921 --> 00:00:22.555
to encompass

00:00:22.555 --> 00:00:25.291
about a third of Jackson's population,

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:27.127
including the densest

00:00:27.127 --> 00:00:28.795
populated white neighborhoods

00:00:28.795 --> 00:00:30.597
and also some of the city's

00:00:30.597 --> 00:00:32.132
most affluent.

00:00:32.132 --> 00:00:32.999
This would also set up

00:00:32.999 --> 00:00:34.034
a separate court system

00:00:34.034 --> 00:00:35.168
for that district.

00:00:35.168 --> 00:00:38.171
Jackson as a whole is 83% black.

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:39.139
Critics of this move

00:00:39.139 --> 00:00:39.406
say it's

00:00:39.406 --> 00:00:41.408
basically the white minority of the city

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:43.076
taking control

00:00:43.076 --> 00:00:44.344
from the black leaders

00:00:44.344 --> 00:00:46.012
of a majority black city.

00:00:46.012 --> 00:00:46.413
It's a move

00:00:46.413 --> 00:00:48.148
the city's mayor has called right racist

00:00:48.148 --> 00:00:49.549
and likened to apartheid

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:50.250
CNN's Omar

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:51.284
Jimenez is live for us

00:00:51.284 --> 00:00:52.185
in Jackson, Mississippi,

00:00:52.185 --> 00:00:53.686
at the state capitol, no more.

00:00:53.686 --> 00:00:55.121
The state Senate has made a few key

00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:56.556
changes to the House bill.

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:57.590
How are residents

00:00:57.590 --> 00:00:59.092
and city leaders reacting

00:00:59.092 --> 00:01:00.026
to those changes?

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:02.662
Yeah, we

00:01:02.662 --> 00:01:03.296
just got out of the

00:01:03.296 --> 00:01:04.664
hearing with some of those residents

00:01:04.664 --> 00:01:05.732
and city leaders.

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:07.100
And really what they said

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:08.134
they were voicing concerns

00:01:08.134 --> 00:01:09.269
about how to address

00:01:09.269 --> 00:01:10.103
public safety

00:01:10.103 --> 00:01:10.870
here in Jackson,

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:12.305
where violence has spiked

00:01:12.305 --> 00:01:13.139
in recent years.

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:13.973
But more specifically,

00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:14.641
they were voicing

00:01:14.641 --> 00:01:16.309
concerns about this bill.

00:01:16.309 --> 00:01:17.911
Now, some of the key changes

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:19.179
from when it was first introduced

00:01:19.179 --> 00:01:19.913
on the House side

00:01:19.913 --> 00:01:21.948
to where it is now on the Senate side

00:01:22.115 --> 00:01:24.150
is rather than having a single district

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:24.884
with these state

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:25.985
appointed judges

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:27.720
and an expanded jurisdiction

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:29.589
of this Capitol Police force.

00:01:29.589 --> 00:01:32.492
That jurisdiction now expands citywide.

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:34.260
You still, though, have the issue

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:35.495
of having judges

00:01:35.495 --> 00:01:38.131
appointed by state leaders,

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:40.233
which in this case are majority white

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:42.569
instead of elected judges in a city

00:01:42.569 --> 00:01:45.004
that is more than 80% black.

00:01:45.038 --> 00:01:46.940
So therein lies one of the major issues.

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:49.209
And that jurisdiction of the Capitol

00:01:49.209 --> 00:01:49.542
Police

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:51.411
force would expand citywide

00:01:51.411 --> 00:01:53.446
meant to strike an agreement

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:54.280
with the Jackson

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:56.116
police force on how to police,

00:01:56.116 --> 00:01:57.750
in theory, together.

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:58.985
So I want you to take a listen

00:01:58.985 --> 00:02:00.687
to the district attorney

00:02:00.687 --> 00:02:03.389
over the area of Jackson,

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:05.125
along with the mother

00:02:05.125 --> 00:02:06.226
of a man

00:02:06.226 --> 00:02:07.026
who was killed

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:08.495
by a Capitol police officer

00:02:08.495 --> 00:02:09.929
and why she believes this

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:11.898
expansion is not a good idea.

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:16.269
It's laughable to talk about

00:02:16.269 --> 00:02:18.605
new bills doing new things.

00:02:18.671 --> 00:02:20.406
We have now addressed the old problems.

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:21.574
The problem is not the police.

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:22.442
The problem is the system

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:23.309
that we're not funding

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:25.311
to actually get the system working,

00:02:25.311 --> 00:02:26.880
because I know there are bills

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:28.348
that is legislate.

00:02:28.348 --> 00:02:30.183
This legislature has introduced

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:32.652
that will expand Capitol Police Authority

00:02:33.887 --> 00:02:36.222
possibly to the entire city of Jackson.

00:02:36.389 --> 00:02:37.891
And that terrifies me.

00:02:37.891 --> 00:02:40.393
It also angers me

00:02:42.562 --> 00:02:44.464
and there is a lot of anger around this.

00:02:44.464 --> 00:02:45.899
You look no further than T-shirts.

00:02:45.899 --> 00:02:46.533
We've seen

00:02:46.533 --> 00:02:47.133
that it's

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:48.468
Jackson versus

00:02:48.468 --> 00:02:49.102
everybody,

00:02:49.102 --> 00:02:50.703
which is how many residents feel

00:02:50.703 --> 00:02:51.871
now, proponents of this bill,

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:53.773
including its Republican sponsors,

00:02:53.773 --> 00:02:55.341
say that this is really needed

00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:55.942
to help

00:02:55.942 --> 00:02:57.977
keep Jackson safer

00:02:57.977 --> 00:02:59.846
and to increase and bolster

00:02:59.846 --> 00:03:01.881
resources towards judges

00:03:01.881 --> 00:03:03.650
in these cases, or a judiciary

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:05.652
that hasn't seen as much investment

00:03:05.652 --> 00:03:07.620
to keep up with the pace

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:08.821
of what they've had to deal with.

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:09.722
But obviously,

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:10.590
opponents of this

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:11.791
say there are better ways

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:13.927
to address those concerns than this.

00:03:13.927 --> 00:03:14.260
All right.

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:16.229
Omar Herman is in Jackson, Mississippi.

00:03:16.229 --> 00:03:16.863
Thanks so much.

00:03:16.863 --> 00:03:18.464
Let's bring in the mayor,

00:03:18.464 --> 00:03:20.633
Chokwe Antar Lumumba.

00:03:20.633 --> 00:03:21.201
Mayor Lumumba,

00:03:21.201 --> 00:03:22.101
thanks so much for joining us.

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:24.237
So the state Senate version of the bill

00:03:24.237 --> 00:03:25.538
would remove the creation

00:03:25.538 --> 00:03:27.273
of this new unelected court system

00:03:27.273 --> 00:03:28.741
for parts of Jackson

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:29.909
where a majority of the city's

00:03:29.909 --> 00:03:31.177
white population lives,

00:03:31.177 --> 00:03:33.479
which would you likened to apartheid.

00:03:33.479 --> 00:03:35.882
But the state Senate version

00:03:35.882 --> 00:03:38.885
does still expand state control over

00:03:38.885 --> 00:03:40.920
other parts of Jackson.

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:42.522
Are you satisfied with the changes

00:03:42.522 --> 00:03:44.190
made to the bill by the state Senate?

00:03:45.692 --> 00:03:46.259
When I think

00:03:46.259 --> 00:03:46.960
about this

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:48.761
bill in both of its forms,

00:03:48.761 --> 00:03:49.662
I think about the legal

00:03:49.662 --> 00:03:50.730
principle of race.

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:52.298
It's a lot quicker,

00:03:52.298 --> 00:03:54.133
which simply means that it is flawed

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:55.935
in its very nature.

00:03:55.935 --> 00:03:58.504
And so even with the changes,

00:03:58.771 --> 00:03:59.806
it is still an attack

00:03:59.806 --> 00:04:01.307
on black leadership.

00:04:01.307 --> 00:04:02.942
It still is a Trojan horse

00:04:02.942 --> 00:04:05.578
cloaked in the notion of public safety,

00:04:06.145 --> 00:04:08.748
where it is not evidence based,

00:04:08.748 --> 00:04:12.652
where it looks to not only fail

00:04:12.652 --> 00:04:13.286
to support

00:04:13.286 --> 00:04:14.254
the needs of the city

00:04:14.254 --> 00:04:16.623
that have been enumerated for many years.

00:04:16.623 --> 00:04:18.925
We have asked the state legislature

00:04:18.925 --> 00:04:19.626
for support

00:04:19.626 --> 00:04:21.461
in terms of ballistic technology

00:04:21.461 --> 00:04:22.695
to close cases.

00:04:22.695 --> 00:04:24.130
We have asked the state

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:26.432
for support of our 21st century

00:04:26.933 --> 00:04:28.067
real time crime center.

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:29.736
That helps officers

00:04:29.736 --> 00:04:32.205
and when a crime is actively in progress.

00:04:32.405 --> 00:04:34.107
We have asked for support

00:04:34.107 --> 00:04:36.309
of violence, interruption programing

00:04:36.743 --> 00:04:38.611
and credible messenger programing

00:04:38.611 --> 00:04:40.113
all which have been denied

00:04:40.113 --> 00:04:41.147
and have have met

00:04:41.147 --> 00:04:43.016
a deliberate indifference

00:04:43.016 --> 00:04:45.752
or willful disregard of Jackson's needs

00:04:46.319 --> 00:04:48.121
in order to have evidence

00:04:48.121 --> 00:04:48.988
based solutions,

00:04:48.988 --> 00:04:50.256
you would need to know

00:04:50.256 --> 00:04:51.557
that the overwhelming

00:04:51.557 --> 00:04:53.192
majority of our violent crimes

00:04:53.192 --> 00:04:55.261
in Jackson are interpersonal.

00:04:55.261 --> 00:04:57.330
And so that is a very difficult matter

00:04:57.330 --> 00:05:00.333
to police And so we're trying to enter,

00:05:01.034 --> 00:05:03.636
intercede or or stop this cycle

00:05:04.103 --> 00:05:05.004
where people are taking

00:05:05.004 --> 00:05:05.938
permanent solutions

00:05:05.938 --> 00:05:07.540
to temporary problems.

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:09.842
And bring other resources

00:05:09.842 --> 00:05:12.312
and other forms of intervention to

00:05:12.345 --> 00:05:14.113
to the table in order for it

00:05:14.113 --> 00:05:15.081
to help our residents.

00:05:15.081 --> 00:05:17.116
One of the bill's chief sponsors,

00:05:17.116 --> 00:05:18.518
State Representative Trey Lamar.

00:05:18.518 --> 00:05:20.653
He denies any racial motivation

00:05:20.653 --> 00:05:21.688
behind the legislation.

00:05:21.688 --> 00:05:23.122
He says the bill is an effort

00:05:23.122 --> 00:05:23.723
to address

00:05:23.723 --> 00:05:25.892
that crime in Jackson is soaring

00:05:25.892 --> 00:05:27.794
and there's a backlog in the courts.

00:05:27.794 --> 00:05:28.561
How do you respond?

00:05:30.063 --> 00:05:31.664
Well, first and foremost,

00:05:31.664 --> 00:05:33.499
we just listen to the testimony

00:05:33.499 --> 00:05:34.400
of Cliff Johnson

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:36.836
today of the MacArthur Justice Foundation

00:05:37.403 --> 00:05:38.938
that did a actual true

00:05:38.938 --> 00:05:40.940
data comparison of the backlogs of

00:05:41.107 --> 00:05:41.874
Hines County

00:05:41.874 --> 00:05:43.376
in comparison to other counties

00:05:43.376 --> 00:05:45.578
in the state of Mississippi to scale.

00:05:45.611 --> 00:05:47.413
What you find is that there isn't

00:05:47.413 --> 00:05:48.715
a significant backlog

00:05:48.715 --> 00:05:50.883
in comparison to other places.

00:05:50.883 --> 00:05:51.584
Cliff Johnson

00:05:51.584 --> 00:05:53.753
also when asked, I'm not Cliff Johnson.

00:05:53.753 --> 00:05:55.955
Trey Lamar, when asked at the dais

00:05:56.255 --> 00:05:57.290
defending his bill

00:05:57.290 --> 00:05:58.591
why he felt that

00:05:58.591 --> 00:06:00.993
judges needed to be appointed rather than

00:06:01.794 --> 00:06:02.929
elected, he said, Well,

00:06:02.929 --> 00:06:05.164
we simply want the best of the best.

00:06:05.164 --> 00:06:05.865
That feeds

00:06:05.865 --> 00:06:07.867
into the notion of inferiority.

00:06:07.867 --> 00:06:09.135
That feeds into the notion

00:06:09.135 --> 00:06:11.170
that this largely majority

00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:11.904
black city

00:06:11.904 --> 00:06:12.905
is not smart enough

00:06:12.905 --> 00:06:14.107
or equipped enough to know

00:06:14.107 --> 00:06:16.042
who best represents them.

00:06:16.042 --> 00:06:19.779
And there is no evidence based rationale

00:06:20.313 --> 00:06:22.715
for for the creation of this district,

00:06:22.982 --> 00:06:23.816
whichever version.

00:06:23.816 --> 00:06:24.283
First of all,

00:06:24.283 --> 00:06:25.952
if you take the first version

00:06:25.952 --> 00:06:27.453
we would need to ask from Trey Lamar

00:06:27.453 --> 00:06:30.556
while his version of the bill selected

00:06:30.556 --> 00:06:31.290
the most densely

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:33.960
populated white portion of the city.

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:36.562
Jackson is 80 85% black,

00:06:36.562 --> 00:06:39.132
but that portion is about 86% encompasses

00:06:39.132 --> 00:06:42.101
86% of the white population of Jackson.

00:06:42.402 --> 00:06:44.871
Was that by mere happenstance?

00:06:44.871 --> 00:06:47.240
There are no state facilities

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:48.841
within that district.

00:06:48.841 --> 00:06:49.942
And so, you know,

00:06:49.942 --> 00:06:51.677
he is using the Trojan horse

00:06:51.677 --> 00:06:53.579
that has been used historically

00:06:53.579 --> 00:06:54.781
on a number of occasions.

00:06:54.781 --> 00:06:56.549
In order to disenfranchize

00:06:56.549 --> 00:06:58.384
and in order to abuse

00:06:58.384 --> 00:06:59.919
largely black populations.

00:06:59.919 --> 00:07:01.621
What would you say to a constituent

00:07:01.621 --> 00:07:02.321
who says, Mr.

00:07:02.321 --> 00:07:04.424
Mayor, I hear you and I agree.

00:07:04.424 --> 00:07:06.292
I don't I don't trust the motivation

00:07:06.292 --> 00:07:07.393
of these individuals.

00:07:07.393 --> 00:07:09.662
But Jackson recorded

00:07:09.662 --> 00:07:11.397
the highest murder rate in the country

00:07:11.397 --> 00:07:12.665
for a city of over

00:07:12.665 --> 00:07:15.134
100,000 people in 20, 21.

00:07:15.468 --> 00:07:17.870
Crime is a huge problem in Jackson.

00:07:18.971 --> 00:07:20.940
I'd rather have something than nothing.

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:22.008
And they're not going to fund

00:07:22.008 --> 00:07:23.009
what you're asking for.

00:07:23.009 --> 00:07:24.510
This at least would

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:26.546
provide some relief for the police

00:07:27.113 --> 00:07:28.815
that exist in the area

00:07:28.815 --> 00:07:31.350
that will not be included in this.

00:07:31.350 --> 00:07:31.984
Yeah,

00:07:32.051 --> 00:07:32.885
but what I would say

00:07:32.885 --> 00:07:35.087
is that their concern is the my concern.

00:07:35.087 --> 00:07:36.522
And that is why

00:07:36.522 --> 00:07:38.424
we continue to look for new solutions.

00:07:38.424 --> 00:07:38.925
That is why

00:07:38.925 --> 00:07:41.160
we not only recruit more officers,

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:42.528
but talk about and build

00:07:42.528 --> 00:07:43.262
the institutions

00:07:43.262 --> 00:07:44.430
that I've told you about,

00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:45.898
such as our real time

00:07:45.898 --> 00:07:46.566
command center,

00:07:46.566 --> 00:07:47.200
which we've done

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:48.901
through our own resources.

00:07:48.901 --> 00:07:50.803
We've joined in with Wells

00:07:50.803 --> 00:07:52.638
Fargo Bank and National League of Cities

00:07:52.638 --> 00:07:53.673
to create an office

00:07:53.673 --> 00:07:54.841
of violence prevention

00:07:54.841 --> 00:07:56.108
and trauma recovery

00:07:56.108 --> 00:07:58.411
so that for every new officer out

00:07:58.411 --> 00:08:00.279
west, we're bringing on new officers,

00:08:00.279 --> 00:08:01.047
we're bringing on

00:08:01.047 --> 00:08:02.515
additional interventions,

00:08:02.515 --> 00:08:03.850
bringing in social workers

00:08:03.850 --> 00:08:05.284
and mental health experts

00:08:05.284 --> 00:08:06.452
to help curtail

00:08:06.452 --> 00:08:07.320
some of the challenges

00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:08.855
that we see in our community.

00:08:08.855 --> 00:08:10.022
Our sharpest rise

00:08:10.022 --> 00:08:11.257
in violence has been among

00:08:11.257 --> 00:08:12.758
our youngest demographic.

00:08:12.758 --> 00:08:14.227
And so instead of doing a curfew

00:08:14.227 --> 00:08:16.329
where there isn't detention centers

00:08:16.329 --> 00:08:17.129
to hold people,

00:08:17.129 --> 00:08:18.531
nor does it truly get to the root

00:08:18.531 --> 00:08:19.665
cause of why

00:08:19.665 --> 00:08:21.567
young people may find themselves

00:08:21.567 --> 00:08:23.703
in vulnerable places at vulnerable times.

00:08:24.103 --> 00:08:26.772
How do we have people who are specialized

00:08:26.973 --> 00:08:27.740
in the area

00:08:27.740 --> 00:08:29.842
of working with that population

00:08:29.842 --> 00:08:31.177
so that we teach, train

00:08:31.177 --> 00:08:32.879
and support young people

00:08:32.879 --> 00:08:33.412
that they don't

00:08:33.412 --> 00:08:34.881
take permanent solutions

00:08:34.881 --> 00:08:36.616
to their temporary problems?

00:08:36.616 --> 00:08:38.017
We can talk about it continue,

00:08:38.017 --> 00:08:39.685
not only in addition to the things

00:08:39.685 --> 00:08:40.653
that I mentioned,

00:08:40.653 --> 00:08:41.420
other supports

00:08:41.420 --> 00:08:43.489
that help our police department,

00:08:43.489 --> 00:08:44.790
but what we don't want to do

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:45.424
in a moment of

00:08:45.424 --> 00:08:47.493
crisis is reach for a solution

00:08:47.493 --> 00:08:48.060
which is worse

00:08:48.060 --> 00:08:49.462
than where we find ourselves.

00:08:49.462 --> 00:08:49.695
All right.

00:08:49.695 --> 00:08:51.564
Jackson Mayor Chokwe Antar Lumumba,

00:08:51.564 --> 00:08:52.164
thank you so much.

